      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. So the 'Connoisseur' is more about those established Western or East Asian lineages, while the 'Trendsetter' is the multicultural group. \n\nTo be honest, that feels like a very specific split. If we're planning the high-budget visual campaigns, we need to avoid any risk of looking \"cheap\" or \"mass-market.\" In your experience with luxury branding, is there a reason why the most \"sophisticated\" or \"high-status\" tier usually leans towards those specific Western or East Asian backgrounds? Like, are there certain demographics that just don't align with the 'quiet luxury' aesthetic we're going for? I want to make sure our creative direction doesn't inadvertently target groups that might actually dilute the brand's prestige.",
